# Negative test: every GMN logic-glyph-plane term marked in scope
# (gmeow:gmnGlyphInScope true) MUST be RENDERED — reached from a GMN sign either
# directly (an adopted glyph or named-key candidate through gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget,
# or a dictionary alias through gmeow:gmnDictionaryEntryTerm) or COMPOSITIONALLY as a
# declared operand / assembly node of a signed structured operator. An in-scope term
# with no rendering path at all is an uncovered glyph-plane gap: a downstream reader
# would meet a canonical term the notation cannot write. Any returned row is that gap.
#
# The denominator is the in-scope set MINUS the two non-result information states
# (logic:InfoUndetermined, logic:InfoNotEvaluated) that Task 1 rules gmnGlyphNamedKeyRuled
# — the raw Belnap algebra has no value for them, so a coverage anti-join must not
# false-fire on them. Two in-scope terms are covered COMPOSITIONALLY, not by a standalone
# sign, and are exempted by their real structural links, not by name:
#   * logic:antecedent — it heads no denotation of its own (the → arrow denotes the
#     implication on logic:consequent), but it is the paired operand of an implication
#     guard (logic:trigger) whose required companion logic:consequent IS signed, so the
#     antecedent is rendered whenever an implication is written.
#   * logic:Sequent — a reified proof-obligation node CLASS assembled by its signed
#     turnstile operators (⊢ logic:derives, ⊨ logic:entails), not an atomic sign; an
#     owl:Class is a structural node, never given a standalone glyph.
# Every other in-scope term binds a candidate or a dictionary alias, so this returns no rows.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>

SELECT ?t WHERE {
    ?t gmeow:gmnGlyphInScope true .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?t gmeow:gmnGlyphNamedKeyRuled true }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget ?t }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?d gmeow:gmnDictionaryEntryTerm ?t }
    # compositional coverage: the paired operand of a signed structured operator
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
        ?constraint logic:trigger ?t ;
                    logic:requires ?paired .
        ?pairedCand gmeow:gmnCandidateTarget ?paired .
    }
    # compositional coverage: a reified node class assembled by its signed operators
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?t a owl:Class }
}
ORDER BY ?t
